The '''Academy of Fine Arts Vienna''' ({{langx|de|Akademie der bildenden Künste Wien}}) is a public [[art school]] in [[Vienna]], [[Austria]]. Founded in 1688 as a private academy, it is now a public university with more than 1,500 students and six institutes. Its main building on Vienna's Schillerplatz near the [[Ringstrasse|Ringstraße]] boulevard was planned by [[Theophil Hansen]] and inaugurated in 1877. The academy houses an expansive art collection that includes the [[The Last Judgment (Bosch, Vienna)|Last Judgement Triptych]] by [[Hieronymus Bosch]] and is open to the public.

